<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="7cab3a02"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="569e1b94">&lt;p&gt;
    Backlog items:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Should follow the &lt;a class=&quot;elementLink&quot;
        href=&quot;./../../core.mgmt.common.base/guidances/concepts/invest_A1AE8F8B.html&quot;
        guid=&quot;_bD9IsDN_EeiQe93m5lGAfw&quot;&gt;INVEST&lt;/a&gt; concept
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Are the smallest unit of work in that decomposing these items results in smaller Backlog Items
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Should be short, crisp, and easily understood by all parties from the team responsible for development to the
        client stakeholders
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        May be refined which may result in a change to either the description or acceptance criteria, thereby requiring a
        decision as to whether the Backlog Item needs to be re-estimated
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Exhibit varying levels of granularity and this level of detail evolves over time 
        &lt;ul&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                Backlog Items scheduled for the next sprint tend to be smaller and better understood that those which will
                be worked on in later sprints&lt;br /&gt;
            &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="939c6e8e"></attribute>
<attribute name="usageGuidance" nodeId="ab6aa11d"></attribute>
<attribute name="refinedDescription" nodeId="508cf1b1">&lt;p&gt;
    Each item is once implemented is expected to yield a contribution to the value of the overall product, regardless of
    the order in which it is implemented. Value may be in the form of new functionality or feature of the product,
    enhancement to existing functionality, issue fix, or acquired knowledge about the product or processes.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Backlog Items can take numerous forms, some include:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;User Stories -&lt;/strong&gt; Explanation of an end user&apos;s need for the product, which is typically structured
        into a short, simple description of the user&apos;s needs from their perspective.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;Features -&lt;/strong&gt; A capability or functionality of the product that provides value to the end-user. They
        typically serve as an alternative to documenting requirements in the form of user stories.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;Epics -&lt;/strong&gt; A need or requirement that is too big to be estimated and/or is not understood well enough
        for the team to begin working on it. Epics are typically broken down into individual user stories or features for
        the team to be able to estimate and work on the item.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;Themes -&lt;/strong&gt; A collection of epics, requiring multiple decompositions to reach a level of work that
        can be estimated and executed.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;Experiments&lt;/strong&gt; - Work that is added to the backlog to validate assumptions or otherwise mitigate
        risks by learning more about either the process, product, or final users.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;Process Improvements&lt;/strong&gt; - Typically a result of retrospectives or other means of evaluating team
        progress and success to date. Process improvements are any actionable items that are added to the backlog to
        improve the team&apos;s processes.  This may include changes related to people, processes, tools, etc.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;Actions to Remove Impediments-&lt;/strong&gt; Steps that can be taken to unblock the team and allow them to
        progress in their work. When impediments arise, they are escalated and actionable resolutions are added as a
        Backlog Item in the Product Backlog, provided their removal requires significant effort from the team.&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
</Element>
